{"seq":1,"slug":"foundations","title":"基础","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/philosophy-of-probability/foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"why-interpret-probability","title":"为何要解释概率","url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/philosophy-of-probability/foundations/why-interpret-probability","wordCount":2113,"readingTime":9},{"seq":2,"slug":"axioms-vs-meaning","title":"公理与意义之别","url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/philosophy-of-probability/foundations/axioms-vs-meaning","wordCount":2136,"readingTime":9},{"seq":3,"slug":"interpretation-taxonomy","title":"解释谱系","url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/philosophy-of-probability/foundations/interpretation-taxonomy","wordCount":1841,"readingTime":8}],"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"基础\">基础</h1><p>概率演算是数学中少有的「公式毫无争议、含义争吵百年」的分支。工程师、赌徒、量子物理学家、保险精算师都在用同一套贝叶斯定理，却对自己算出的那个数字指什么各执一词。本章的任务，是把这场争吵的根基摆清楚，让后面三章的具体解释有一个共同的问题背景。</p>\n<p>第一篇 <a href=\"why-interpret-probability\">为何解释概率</a> 回答「为什么不能只满足于数学公理」：柯尔莫哥洛夫公理是一套语法，它告诉你概率如何相加相乘，却不告诉你 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0.7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P(A)=0.7</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.7</span></span></span></span></span> 在世界上对应什么。我们会引入萨尔蒙的三条评判标准——可确认性、可应用性、可接纳性——作为衡量任何一种解释成败的标尺。</p>\n<p>第二篇 <a href=\"axioms-vs-meaning\">公理与意义之别</a> 深入形式层：完整陈述柯尔莫哥洛夫三公理、条件概率定义、以及考克斯定理与荷兰赌这两条「反向」路径——它们不预设概率含义，而是从合理性约束反推出概率结构。这是理解「为什么信念度也必须服从概率公理」的关键。</p>\n<p>第三篇 <a href=\"interpretation-taxonomy\">解释谱系</a> 画出全景地图：从拉普拉斯的古典解释出发，沿客观—主观轴展开频率、倾向、逻辑、主观、最佳系统诸种解释，标出它们各自把概率安放在世界、逻辑还是心灵中。它是后两章的导航图，每种解释的深讲都在对应篇章。</p>\n<p>学完本章，你不会得到「哪种解释正确」的答案——那正是全 hub 要慢慢展开的——但你会拥有提问的精确语言和评判的统一标尺。本章是纯概念性的，不需要额外前置，只需对条件概率与贝叶斯定理有基本印象。</p>\n"}